===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|dare||ing-form}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[adventurous|Adventurous]], willing to take on or look for [[risk]]s; [[overbold]].
#: {{syn|en|audacious|dareful|bold|venturesome|adventuresome}}
#* {{RQ:Orczy Miss Elliott|chapter=The Tremarn Case|passage=“There the cause of death was soon ascertained ; the victim of this '''daring''' outrage had been stabbed to death from ear to ear with a long, sharp instrument, in shape like an antique stiletto, which {{...}} was subsequently found under the cushions of the hansom. {{...}}”}}
# [[courageous|Courageous]] or showing [[bravery]]; [[doughty]].
#: {{syn|en|courageous|Thesaurus:brave}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|II|i|text={{...}}By this scimitar,<br>That slew the Sophy and a Persian prince<br>That won three fields of Sultan Solyman,<br>I would outstare the sternest eyes that look,<br>Outbrave the heart most '''daring''' on earth,<br>Pluck the young sucking cubs from the she-bear,<br>Yea, mock the lion when he roars for prey,<br>To win thee, lady. {{...}}}}
# [[racy|Racy]]; sexually [[provocative]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Randy Rawls|title=Best Defense|page=59
|passage=Just what I wanted, seeing my mom in a '''daring''' bikini—or worse yet, my being in one. I had the perfect drawer I could bury it in.}}

